+## TL;DR
+- **Best search stack:** [Meilisearch](https://github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch), [Typesense](https://github.com/typesense/typesense), and [OpenSearch](https://github.com/opensearch-project/OpenSearch) are the strongest open source bases for storefront search, faceting, typo tolerance, and hybrid retrieval.
+- **Best recommendation stack:** [Metarank](https://github.com/metarank/metarank), [RecBole](https://github.com/RUCAIBox/RecBole), and [TorchRec](https://github.com/meta-pytorch/torchrec) cover ranking APIs, experimentation, and large-scale personalization.
+- **Best conversational commerce stack:** [Flowise](https://github.com/FlowiseAI/Flowise), [Langflow](https://github.com/langflow-ai/langflow), [Dify](https://github.com/langgenius/dify), and [Rasa](https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa) are the most practical open repos for support bots, shopping assistants, and agent workflows.
+- **Best generative content stack:** [ComfyUI](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI), [diffusers](https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers), and [Stable Diffusion WebUI](https://github.com/AUTOMATIC1111/stable-diffusion-webui) are the strongest open GitHub options for product imagery, creative testing, and asset generation.
+- **Best demand planning stack:** [Prophet](https://github.com/facebook/prophet), [GluonTS](https://github.com/awslabs/gluonts), [NeuralProphet](https://github.com/ourownstory/neural_prophet), and [PyTorch Forecasting](https://github.com/sktime/pytorch-forecasting) are the most established open source choices for forecasting promotions, inventory, and seasonality.
+
+## Why This List
+Most “AI tools for ecommerce” roundups mix closed SaaS, affiliate spam, and vague automation claims. This repository is intentionally stricter: every item here has a public GitHub repository, an inspectable codebase, and a real engineering use case for ecommerce teams building search, personalization, support, creative tooling, or forecasting in-house.
+
+Open source matters here because ecommerce teams need control over catalog data, customer context, ranking logic, model costs, deployment targets, and compliance boundaries. If a repo could not be verified on GitHub, or if it was only a proprietary hosted product, it was excluded.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
+### Search, Retrieval, And Product Discovery
