+#### [Typesense](https://github.com/typesense/typesense)
+> **Description:** Typesense is presented as an open source alternative to Algolia and a simpler alternative to Elasticsearch, with typo-tolerant in-memory search, merchandising-oriented controls, search UI integrations, and strong out-of-the-box relevance. Its README explicitly discusses ecommerce-style tradeoffs against Algolia and Elasticsearch, which makes it especially relevant for storefront use. GitHub showed **25.5k stars**, **C++** as the primary language, a **GPL-3.0** license, and the latest visible commit on **Sep 24, 2025**. It is a pragmatic choice when you want self-hosted, API-first site search without a heavy cluster footprint.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/typesense/typesense](https://github.com/typesense/typesense)
