+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for ecommerce search?
+The strongest GitHub-first options in this list are Meilisearch, Typesense, OpenSearch, Vespa, and Qdrant. The right choice depends on whether you need classic keyword search, hybrid retrieval, or vector-based semantic search.
+
+### Are there truly free AI ecommerce tools with source code on GitHub?
+Yes. Every project in this repository has a public GitHub repository. Some use permissive licenses like MIT or Apache-2.0, while others use GPL, AGPL, BSD, or custom open licenses, so review each repo before commercial deployment.
+
+### What is the best open source recommendation engine for ecommerce?
+For direct ranking and personalization APIs, Metarank is one of the clearest ecommerce fits. For experimentation and model research, RecBole, TorchRec, implicit, and LightFM are strong options depending on scale and modeling depth.
+
+### Which GitHub AI tools can help build an ecommerce chatbot?
+Rasa, Flowise, Langflow, Dify, and Hexabot are the strongest repos here for conversational commerce. Rasa is best for structured assistants, while Flowise, Langflow, and Dify are better for agent workflows and LLM-heavy experiences.
+
+### What open source AI tools can generate product images or ad creatives?
+diffusers, ComfyUI, Fooocus, and Stable Diffusion WebUI are the best verified GitHub repos in this list for image generation. ComfyUI is strongest for reusable workflows, while diffusers is strongest for code-driven pipelines.
+
+### Are there open source AI tools for ecommerce demand forecasting?
+Yes. Prophet, NeuralProphet, GluonTS, and PyTorch Forecasting all qualify and have public GitHub repositories. They are useful for sales forecasting, inventory planning, staffing, promotion planning, and seasonality analysis.
+
+### Why are there gaps in some categories?
+Because the list excludes proprietary SaaS, weak “AI” claims, and repos without a public GitHub codebase. Some ecommerce AI categories are dominated by vendors rather than durable open source projects, so the honest result is fewer qualified repos.
+
+## GitHub Search Queries Used
+
